WEBVTT

00:03:29.358 --> 00:03:32.477
into bracelets and necklaces.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:36.556
Ethiopia has had the longest
tradition of writing,

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.875
with the Ethiopic script
that was developed

00:03:38.899 --> 00:03:40.837
in the fourth century A.D.

00:03:40.861 --> 00:03:43.351
and is used to write Amharic,

00:03:43.375 --> 00:03:46.636
which is spoken by over 24 million people.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:51.093
King Ibrahim Njoya of the Bamum
Kingdom of Cameroon

00:03:51.117 --> 00:03:54.658
developed Shü-mom at the age of 25.

00:03:54.682 --> 00:03:56.745
Shü-mom is a writing system.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.738
It's a syllabary. It's not
exactly an alphabet.

00:03:59.762 --> 00:04:03.053
And here we see
three stages of development